    },
    {
      "kind": "url",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash/blob/314113f8a7dadb388215396ba5fbee2c610a04d6/inference/model.py",
      "checkedOn": "2026-11-21"
    },
    {
      "kind": "url",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash/blob/314113f8a7dadb388215396ba5fbee2c610a04d6/inference/kernel.py",
      "checkedOn": "2026-11-21"
    },
    {
      "kind": "url",
      "url": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash/blob/314113f8a7dadb388215396ba5fbee2c610a04d6/inference/engram.py",
      "checkedOn": "2026-11-21"
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "Main text backbone. Large matrices use a BF16 reference except source FP32 operations and the explicitly stored FP8 Engram table with E8M0 scales. Checkpoint FP8/FP4 MoE and projection kernels, vision, DSpark, sampling need separate configurations."
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "BF16 attention caches represent active batch lanes in the reference fake-quant path. Physical cache grows by completed groups and preserves all provisioned local windows. The Engram token history reserves its configured context length; its precomputed token map uses the released embedding vocabulary as an upper bound."
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "CSA2 runs full index dot products before applying the candidate mask, as in the reference implementation. Sparse attention, hash, nonlinear and selection work use explicit analytical operation/traffic proxies. Pair counts use the published candidate dimensions and assume enough candidate entries for final Top-K; logical query chunks extend the reference initial prefill and single-token decode."
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "Local equations bind allocated request, head and expert extents. Lookup and sparse expert reads use explicit traffic equations. Link rates and analytical work proxies describe the configured estimate."
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "Each rank holds whole attention heads and matching output groups. Indexer query heads contribute FP32 partial scores, reduced before candidate selection or masking. Window, compressed latent, index K and compressor state are replicated, with one backing per shared cache on each rank. The row-parallel output partial uses an FP32 AllReduce before resuming the BF16 residual path."
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "Each EP rank owns a contiguous, equal count of routed experts. Each token keeps its global Top-K, with per-rank route budgets balanced by quotient and remainder. Allocated slots use ceil(K/EP). Useful work and sparse gathers use valid slots. The shared expert is replicated and added after reducing FP32 routed partials."
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "The combined V4.1 preset also shards the Engram weight and scale tables by rows, reserving ceil(rows/ranks) rows per rank. The lookup charges one read per requested hash on each rank, including the masked dummy row, and reduces the BF16 values before the replicated projection."
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "Routed-expert TP shards matched gate and up channels, SwiGLU results and down-projection input channels. TP peers within each owner group duplicate its route metadata. FP32 routed partials are summed across owner and feature ranks before the replicated shared expert is added."
    }
  ],
